{"text": "MEDICAL CHRONOLOGY - ATTORNEY WORK PRODUCT\nPrepared for: Tucker Royce, Royce & Maldonado-Byrd, LLP            Firm file: RMB-24-0612\nPrepared by: Gwendolyn Spratt, RN, BSN, LNCC, Spratt Legal Nurse Consulting     Draft 2, 11/09/2025\nPatient: APPLEWHITE, Vernon L.     DOB: 4/18/1967     MRN (Saint Agnes): SA-00771209\nRecords reviewed: Saint Agnes ED and inpatient (Bates APP-SA-000001 to APP-SA-000412); EMS run report; Wabash Valley Neurology Group; Sugar Creek Rehabilitation Hospital; pharmacy; employer file.\n\nBACKGROUND\nMr. Applewhite, 57 at the time, a long-haul driver. Known history per primary care: hypertension, poorly controlled; atrial fibrillation diagnosed 2022, prescribed apixaban; type 2 diabetes; smoker, one pack a day. Pharmacy fill history shows no apixaban refill after November 2023 (he told his wife it cost too much after he lost insurance).\n\nDATE / TIME        SOURCE (BATES)        EVENT                                                    COMMENT\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n03/09/2024  21:47   EMS run report        Wife, Deborah Applewhite, calls 911 from home,              Onset time documented by EMS\n                   (APP-EMS-0003)        1127 Vigo Street, Terre Haute IN. \"Dizzy, can't walk               as \"approx 21:15.\" This is\n                                         straight, threw up twice.\" BP 198/112. Glucose 164.                the only clear onset time.\n03/09/2024  22:31   ED triage             Triage RN Kristof Nagy. Chief complaint entered as              No stroke scale done at\n                   (APP-SA-000014)       \"vertigo / N&V.\" Triage level 3. No NIHSS recorded.                triage. Policy requires one.\n03/09/2024  23:40   ED physician note     Dr. Cyrus Tehrani. Exam: \"nystagmus, unsteady gait, no             Did not document finger-to-\n                   (APP-SA-000019-22)    focal weakness.\" Impression: peripheral vertigo.                   nose, speech, or visual\n                                         Orders: meclizine, ondansetron, IV fluids. CT head ordered.        fields. A-fib not mentioned.\n3/10/24     00:52   Radiology             CT head without contrast: \"no acute intracranial                   CT is insensitive for\n                   (APP-SA-000031)       abnormality.\" No CTA or MRI ordered.                               posterior strokes.\n3/10/24     02:15   ED nursing note       \"Pt states room still spinning, c/o double vision.\"                 NEW SYMPTOM. Not relayed to\n                   (APP-SA-000027)       RN Nagy. No physician notified per the record.                the physician per the chart.\n3/10/24     03:05   Discharge             Discharged home with meclizine. Dx: vertigo (not coded as          Discharged 5 h 50 min after\n                   (APP-SA-000033)       stroke). Instructions: follow up with PCP in 3 days.               onset; inside any extended\n                                         Mrs. Applewhite signed; pt \"too dizzy to sign.\"                  window for evaluation.\nMarch 10, 2024  11:20   EMS / ED (second visit)   Found on bathroom floor by wife. Slurred speech, left facial droop, cannot swallow.\n                   (APP-SA-000040)       NIHSS 14 on arrival. 17 hours after first triage.\n3/10/24     12:02   MRI brain             Acute infarct, left cerebellum and lateral medulla; basilar artery thrombus.\n                   (APP-SA-000058)       Posterior circulation stroke. ICD-10 I63.9 used.\n3/10/24     12:40   Neurology consult     Dr. Folasade Akintola (Wabash Valley Neurology). \"Outside            Her note is the key\n                   (APP-SA-000061-64)    t-PA window.         causation document.\n                                         Presentation last night was, in retrospect, a posterior circulation event.\" Transferred to ICU.\n3/10 - 3/29/24      Inpatient             ICU 6 days. PEG tube placed 3/14. Aspiration pneumonia 3/17.      19-day admission. Charges\n                   (APP-SA-000070-398)   Speech, PT, OT daily.                                              $214,880.16.\n29 Mar 2024 -       Sugar Creek Rehab   Inpatient rehabilitation under Dr. Marguerite Duchesne.              Rehab charges $96,412.00.\nMay 17, 2024       (APP-SC-0001-0220)    Discharge status:\n                                         wheelchair for distance, walker in home, pureed diet, persistent double vision, left-sided ataxia.\nSept. 2024          Neurology follow-up   Dr. Akintola: \"plateaued.\" Depression, started sertraline.          Permanent restrictions.\n                   (APP-WV-0012)         Cannot return to commercial driving; CDL medical card\n                                         surrendered.\n10/2024            Employer file         Terminated after exhausting leave. Last gross annual pay           Lost earnings base.\n                                         $71,340. Applied for SSDI; awarded effective September 2024,\n                                         $2,214 per month.\n\nNURSE CONSULTANT'S OBSERVATIONS (not opinions on the standard of care)\n1. No stroke scale at either triage or physician evaluation on the first visit, despite vomiting, gait instability, severe hypertension and a charted history of atrial fibrillation in the hospital's own prior records (visit of 8/2/2022, APP-SA-000405).\n2. The 02:15 nursing note of new double vision was not escalated. Mr. Nagy was a travel nurse on his third shift at the facility; ask for his orientation file.\n3. Dr. Tehrani was covering the ED alone with 31 patients on the board at 23:00 per the tracking log (APP-SA-000409).\n4. Defense will raise the stopped apixaban and the smoking. Note also one prior ED visit (12/31/2023) where the chart records \"ETOH on breath\"; nothing similar on 3/9.\n5. Missing: audit trail for the triage record; I count two edits on 3/10 after the second arrival. Request metadata.\n\nClient contact for questions on home care: Deborah, 812-555-0146 (she works nights at the candle factory; call before 2 pm).\nInvoice for this draft: 14.5 hours at $165 = $2,392.50.   G. Spratt", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "711 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Vernon L. Applewhite", "Gwendolyn Spratt", "Deborah Applewhite", "Kristof Nagy", "Dr. Cyrus Tehrani", "Mrs. Applewhite", "Dr. Folasade Akintola", "Dr. Marguerite Duchesne", "Dr. Akintola", "Mr. Nagy", "Deborah"], "companies": ["Tucker Royce", "Royce & Maldonado-Byrd, LLP", "Saint Agnes", "Wabash Valley Neurology Group", "Sugar Creek Rehabilitation Hospital", "EMS", "Wabash Valley Neurology", "Sugar Creek Rehab", "Employer", "candle factory"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Terre Haute", "Sugar Creek Rehab", "candle factory"], "health": ["hypertension", "atrial fibrillation", "apixaban", "type 2 diabetes", "vertigo", "N&V", "glucose", "BP", "peripheral vertigo", "nystagmus", "unsteady gait", "stroke", "NIHSS", "double vision", "left facial droop", "cannot swallow", "acetate", "A-fib", "plateaued", "depression", "pureed diet", "left-sided ataxia"], "sensitive": ["travel nurse"], "names": ["Vernon L", "Deborah", "Cyrus", "Kristof", "Nagy", "Folasade", "Marguerite", "Mr. Nagy", "Dr. Tehrani", "G. Spratt"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 3, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.29999999701976776, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 57, "end": 63, "text": "Tucker", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Tucker Royce"}, {"start": 64, "end": 98, "text": "Royce, Royce & Maldonad